# Backend API And Services

- Keep controllers thin: parse request input, call services, and map to HTTP responses; keep business logic in service modules.
- Validate external input at boundaries: treat request body/query/params/headers as untrusted; sanitize/validate before persistence or downstream use.
- Follow existing auth/session flow: reuse patterns from auth plugin and shared guards (`authenticate`, `requireAuthenticated`) instead of bespoke auth logic.
- Preserve response contracts: keep `ok/data/error` conventions and existing status code semantics unless explicitly asked to change them.
- Reuse centralized utilities: prefer shared helpers in `apps/api/src/utils` and repository/service patterns in `apps/api/src/modules`.
- Do not swallow errors: either map to explicit domain/auth errors or log and rethrow using established logging style.
- Keep Prisma access in repository/service paths, not scattered across route handlers.
